    lower: rule G, a generic function seen as a generic slot is related as tsc relates it, the slot's type parameters held opaque and the source instantiated in their context; an instantiation holding any where the slot doesn't stops (#7fd51gk)
    
    widened's signature branch instantiated a generic source only for a target
    with no type parameters, so a generic provider against a generic slot was
    related raw: @types/node's setTimeout<TArgs> seen as sys.ts's
    <A>(callback: (...args: NoInfer<A>) => void, ms, ...args: A) compared TArgs
    with A and refused both ways at sys.ts 1501 and 1599. Now any single generic
    source signature whose type parameters aren't the target's is instantiated in
    the context of the target's canonical signature (relater.go's own steps), and
    the walk below is unchanged.
    
    Condition 3: a source type parameter the target doesn't fix falls back to its
    constraint; one holding any would let the walk accept anything, so when the
    instantiation puts any where the target has a type and the raw source didn't
    (signatureAny), it's NotYet. This also guards the older generic-to-plain branch.
    
    widenedProperties' generic-method stop (#q6gs98r) now relates one signature on
    each side through widened, so g1, g4 to g7 and the Box row are refused at the
    narrowed parameter, and an overload set (o2) still stops unjudged.
    
    Pins: TestASetTimeoutProviderIsRelatedThroughTheNoInferSlot,
    TestAGenericMethodWithANarrowerConstraintAndTheViewsParametersLowers (i2),
    TestAGenericFunctionWhoseSlotDoesntFixItsTypeParameterIsNotYet (L2), and the
    generic-method rows' new texts.
    
